menu "Application"

    config APP_BRINGUP_STORE_TEST
        bool "Bring-up: run a storage round-trip test at boot"
        default y
        help
            Exercises NVS + SPIFFS: creates a profile, a button and a hotkey,
            exports everything into a RAM bundle, wipes the store, imports the
            bundle back and verifies the data including the raw frame bytes.
            WARNING: it begins with a factory reset and therefore erases any
            stored profiles. Disable it once the storage layer is trusted.

    config APP_BRINGUP_IR_TX_BLINK
        bool "Bring-up: blink the IR emitter pin before anything else"
        default y
        help
            Drives the emitter pin at 2.5 Hz with no carrier for about 20 seconds.
            Watch the IR LED through a phone camera: it must BLINK. A steady glow
            means you are looking at a power indicator LED, not the emitter, or
            that the emitter is not driven by the configured pin.

    config APP_BRINGUP_IR_LOOPBACK
        bool "Bring-up: run an IR transmit-to-receive loopback test at boot"
        default y
        help
            Emits a synthetic frame through the IR emitter and checks whether the
            receiver picks it up. Validates the emitter, the receiver, both RMT
            channels and the 38 kHz carrier without a remote control or a user
            present. Requires the emitter to be visible to the receiver.

    config APP_BRINGUP_IR_LEARN
        bool "Bring-up: auto-arm IR learning at boot"
        default y
        help
            Temporary bring-up aid for the ir_capture milestone. Arms the IR
            receiver for a short window after boot and logs the captured frames so
            the driver can be validated without the dashboard. Disable this once
            learning is driven over BLE.

    config APP_BRINGUP_IR_LEARN_WINDOW_MS
        int "Bring-up learn window (ms)"
        depends on APP_BRINGUP_IR_LEARN
        range 5000 600000
        default 180000
        help
            Generous by default so a bench session does not depend on pressing a
            remote within a few seconds of reset. Every captured frame restarts
            the window, and a reset reopens it.

endmenu
